course: dictionary
lesson: 1011
title: One word, two jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words can be a thing or an action. Bone can be a noun, one of the hard parts inside a body, or a verb, meaning to take the bones out. Context tells you which one. «A newborn baby has more bones than an adult.» Here bones are things, so this is a noun.
explain: Check the words around the word. If you can put «a» or «the» in front of it, it is probably a noun. If you can put «to» in front of it, it is probably a verb: to bone a fish means to take the bones out.
fact: Bone is a noun when it means one of the hard, white parts inside a body, such as «a bone» or «bones».
fact: Bone is a verb when it means to take the bones out, as in «to bone a fish».
fact: An adult human has 206 bones, which hold up the body and protect the organs.
fact: «A cast is a hard shell of plaster or fibreglass that stops a broken bone moving while it heals.»
fact: «Bone dry» means completely dry, and «a bone to pick with you» means you have a complaint.
exercise: In «A newborn baby has more bones than an adult», what kind of word is bones? | *A noun, a thing in the body | A place where babies sleep | A verb, an action | An adjective, describing a baby
exercise: Mum says, «Please bone the fish before we eat.» What does bone mean here? | *To take the bones out | To break a bone | To cook it very slowly | To count the bones
exercise: «Never jump from high walls or roofs for a dare; falls can break bones or worse.» What can falls from high walls do? | Make you hungry | *Break bones or worse | Make you taller | Help you fly
test: «A cast stops a broken bone moving while it heals.» What does a cast do? | Keeps the bone wet | *Stops the bone moving while it heals | Takes the bones out | Makes the bone grow longer
test: The skull protects the brain, and the ribs protect the heart and lungs. What does the skull protect? | The lungs | *The brain | The heart | The ribs
exam: Which sentence uses bone as a verb? | *Please bone the chicken before we eat. | A newborn baby has more bones than an adult. | Dogs love to chew bones. | The skeleton has many bones inside.
